    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d214">

                <pb facs="0491" n="395" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg395"/>

                <head>No. 212.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wing
                        to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Quito,
                                Ecuador</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-03-30"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 30, 1874</date>.
                        (Received April 28.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 382.</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have this day sent to the government of
                    Ecuador a copy of the “act authorizing coinage to be executed at the mints of
                    the United States for foreign countries.”</p>
                <p>I presume that this government will eventually desire to avail itself of the
                    benefit of this act.</p>
                <p>No. 1 is a copy of my communication to Minister Leon.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>RUMSEY WING.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian"
                                when="1874-04-01"><hi rendition="#small-caps">April</hi>
                            1</date>.</dateline></opener>
                    <p>P. S.—I have just received an official note from Minister Leon, of which 1
                        and 2 are copy and translation.</p>
                    <closer><signed>R. W.</signed></closer>
                </postscript>




                <xi:include href="d214-a1.xml" xpointer="d214-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d214-a2.xml" xpointer="d214-a2"/>
            </div>
